{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y8kfCiDzSagbxtXqLLNNon","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Result\n\"Software developer Graydon Hoare created Rust in 2006 while working at Mozilla, which officially sponsored the project in 2009. The first stable release, Rust 1.0, was published in May 2015. The project has been sponsored by the Rust Foundation since February 2021. It has been adopted by many software projects, especially web services and system software. It has been studied academically and has a growing community of developers.\\n\\nDevelopment focused on finalizing features for version 1.0 (which would begin providing backward compatibility).[22]: 41:26  According to Andrew Binstock writing for Dr. Dobb's Journal in January 2014, while Rust was \\\"widely viewed as a remarkably elegant language\\\", adoption slowed because it radically changed from version to version.[30]\\n\\nOn May 15, 2015, Rust 1.0 became the first stable release.[21] One year later, the compiler had accumulated at least 1,400 contributors, and there were at least 5,000 third-party libraries published on the package management website Crates.io.[22]: 43:15 \"\n### Ran Playwright code\n```js\nawait page.evaluate('() => Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(\\'p\\')).filter(p => /1\\\\.0/.test(p.innerText)).slice(0, 3).map(p => p.innerText.slice(0, 1200)).join(\\'\\\\n\\\\n\\')');\n```"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63315cb6-276c-46b3-b774-0637874f82f4","uuid":"eb6fcfe0-ceaf-4d16-83a2-d98e96a570ec","timestamp":"2026-10-29T13:40:10.400Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"### Result\n\"Software developer Graydon Hoare created Rust in 2006 while working at Mozilla, which officially sponsored the project in 2009. The first stable release, Rust 1.0, was published in May 2015. The project has been sponsored by the Rust Foundation since February 2021. It has been adopted by many software projects, especially web services and system software. It has been studied academically and has a growing community of developers.\\n\\nDevelopment focused on finalizing features for version 1.0 (which would begin providing backward compatibility).[22]: 41:26  According to Andrew Binstock writing for Dr. Dobb's Journal in January 2014, while Rust was \\\"widely viewed as a remarkably elegant language\\\", adoption slowed because it radically changed from version to version.[30]\\n\\nOn May 15, 2015, Rust 1.0 became the first stable release.[21] One year later, the compiler had accumulated at least 1,400 contributors, and there were at least 5,000 third-party libraries published on the package management website Crates.io.[22]: 43:15 \"\n### Ran Playwright code\n```js\nawait page.evaluate('() => Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(\\'p\\')).filter(p => /1\\\\.0/.test(p.innerText)).slice(0, 3).map(p => p.innerText.slice(0, 1200)).join(\\'\\\\n\\\\n\\')');\n```"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Y8kfCiDzSagbxtXqLLNNon","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
